{0 jmap}

{!modules: Jmap Jmap_eio Jmap_top}

{1 Tutorial}

See the {!page-tutorial} for a comprehensive guide to using JMAP with OCaml,
including how types map to JSON and practical examples.

The {!page-coverage} page is a matrix of every RFC 8620 and RFC 8621 method
against the codecs, builders, unit tests, oracle tests and runnable examples
that exercise it. The directories under [examples/] are a second tutorial,
a profile setup step, protocol steps and larger programs, each with runnable
code and a README. [scripts/run-examples.sh] runs them against a configured
server. The profile setup also lists and saves logins offline.

See {!page-profiles} for saving a shared login and using [--profile] or
[JMAP_PROFILE] throughout the examples. [examples/q-events/] demonstrates
{!Jmap_eio.Push.next} and subscription completion.

{1 The Eio client}

{!Jmap_eio} is the client. {!Jmap_eio.Auth} holds the credential,
{!Jmap_eio.Transport} the HTTP stack, {!Jmap_eio.Client} the session and the
requests, {!Jmap_eio.Profile} the shared named-login store, {!Jmap_eio.Sync}
paging and change draining, and {!Jmap_eio.Push} the event source. A chain of
method calls is sent and read by
{!Jmap_eio.Client.val-call} when it ends in one handle and by
{!Jmap_eio.Client.run} when it ends in several. Its module page opens with a
quick start.
